L000496	{\it \noindent \textbf{Non-relativistic media --}} In the regime where the microscopic dynamics are nonrelativistic in the rest frame (so that $w\!\ll\!1$), the usual time--dilation intuition is recovered: the bounds collapse to $a/\gamma \le i\omega' \le b/\gamma$. Indeed, in this limit, the boosted eigenvalue equation $i\gamma\omega'(1{+}v \E^1)\Psi = \s\Psi$ simplifies to $i\gamma\omega'\Psi = \s\Psi$, implying that $\gamma\omega'$ matches a corresponding rest--frame nonhydrodynamic frequency.
