L000818	\section*{Breakdown of quasi-hydrodynamics at large boosts}
L000819	
L000820	We consider a rest-frame model of the form $(\partial_t+\E^1\partial_x+\s)\Psi=0$, with $\Psi\in\mathbb{C}^D$, whose maximal signal velocity is, say, $w\,{=}\,1/2$, and whose rest-frame non-hydrodynamic spectrum exhibits a gap $a=1$. According to Theorem~2, after a boost with velocity $v$, the non-hydrodynamic frequencies retain a minimal gap $a'=(1-|v|/2)/\gamma$.
L000821	
L000822	We now introduce an extended model $\big[\partial_t+\E^1_{(+2)}\partial_x+\s_{(+2)}\big]\Psi_{(+2)}=0$, with $\Psi_{(+2)}\in\mathbb{C}^{D+2}$, defined by
L000823	\begin{equation}\label{quasuzzo}
L000824	\E^1_{(+2)} = \left[\begin{array}{c|cc}
L000825	\E^1 & 0 & 0 \\
L000826	\hline
L000827	0 & 1 & 0 \\
L000828	0 & 0 & -1
L000829	\end{array}\right]\,,
L000830	\qquad\qquad
L000831	\s_{(+2)} = \left[\begin{array}{c|cc}
L000832	\s & 0 & 0 \\
L000833	\hline
L000834	0 & \lambda & 0 \\
L000835	0 & 0 & \lambda
L000836	\end{array}\right]\qquad\qquad (\text{with }0<\lambda\ll 1)\, .
L000837	\end{equation}
L000838	This extension amounts to adding two non-hydrodynamic degrees of freedom that propagate at the speed of light and decay parametrically slowly, with rate $\lambda$, in the rest frame.
L000839	In a frame moving with velocity $v$, the non-hydrodynamic spectrum of this extended model coincides with that of the original system, supplemented by two additional modes,
L000840	\begin{equation}
L000841	i\omega'_{\pm}=\dfrac{\lambda}{\gamma(1\pm v)} \, .
L000842	\end{equation}
L000843	These modes lie in the quasi-hydrodynamic regime as long as they remain well separated from the rest of the spectrum. This separation breaks down when $|v|\gtrsim 1-2\lambda$. Therefore, regardless of how small $\lambda$ is, there always exists an observer $\mathcal{O}'$ for whom no quasi-hydrodynamic spectral separation is present at $k'=0$. In the limit $\lambda\to0$, such an observer must move increasingly close to the speed of light.
